  "verbalization": "Bexarotene is a retinoid compound that is included in the broader class of retinoids, which includes Tazarotene and Acitretin. These retinoids are known to bind to the RXRB receptor, a key component of the retinoic acid receptor signaling pathway. This binding is supported by multiple paths in the dataset, all of which indicate a direct interaction between retinoids and Rxrb. The shared lowest common ancestors across these paths—such as Bexarotene, Retinoids, and Retinoic Acid Agent—suggest a common biological function and a consistent mechanism of action. The evidence from these paths collectively supports the hypothesis that Bexarotene exerts its effects through a retinoic acid receptor (RXRB) binding mechanism, which is a well-established pathway in retinoid-based therapies. The high scores in the final scores indicate a strong and consistent relationship, reinforcing the mechanistic link between Bexarotene and Rxrb.",
